 Logs are written to `logs/rsl_rl/z1_flat/{timestamp}_{run_name}/`. Checkpoints are saved every 500 iterations (see
 `Z1FlatPPORunnerCfg.save_interval`).
 
+#### Multi-motion boxing training
+
+Pass a directory to train one policy on every `.npz` file in it. Motions remain separate; each motion is divided into
+approximately one-second bins for sampling and difficulty scoring. Rollouts continue across adjacent bins in the same
+motion and reset only on a hard failure, source-motion end, or episode timeout, so inter-bin transitions are trained.
+Two thirds of reset environments traverse a shuffled full-coverage queue, while up to one third replay bins from the
+failure pool. A bin enters after 15 soft tracking failures or 2 hard falls, and exits after 5 consecutive successful
+trials. Successful trials outside the pool decrement stale failure evidence. The curriculum state is stored in
+checkpoints. The Z1 task starts with mild friction, mass, reset-state, and observation randomization; COM shifts and
+external pushes remain disabled for this first stage.
+
+```bash
+python scripts/rsl_rl/train.py \
+  --task=Tracking-Flat-Z1-v0 \
+  --motion_dir source/whole_body_tracking/whole_body_tracking/datasets/boxing-dataset-magiclab-z1/train_npz \
+  --num_envs 256 --max_iterations 30000 --headless \
+  --logger tensorboard --run_name boxing_multi_v1
+```
+
+TensorBoard event files are written into the run directory. When training finishes normally, the numerically latest
+`model_*.pt` is reloaded and exported to `<run>/exported/policy.onnx`; its checkpoint path is embedded in the ONNX
+metadata as `source_checkpoint`.
+
